// PARAM: --analysis interval --solver warrow-per-origin --context entry-state
// warrow-per-origin under entry-state contexts. Each entered state is its
// own context, so p(1) and p(2) never share a FunctionEntry seed and the
// update rule has nothing to widen across origins: both activations stay
// exact. Locks in that the combination is routed at all -- the resolver
// accepts every solver at every Interval context, and the dispatcher must
// match every plan the resolver produces.
void p(int32 n) {
  __voblint_check(n < 10) // PROVED
}
void main() {
  p(1);
  p(2)
}
